# Frontend Rules

Read `docs/04_SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/10_UI_SYSTEM.md`, and `docs/11_COMPONENT_LIBRARY.md`.

## Server vs Client

- Default to Server Components — no `"use client"` unless required
- Client Components for: forms with pending state, modals, theme toggle, Framer Motion, toasts
- Fetch data in Server Components; pass serializable props to Client Components
- Use `Suspense` + `loading.tsx` for streaming

## Next.js App Router

- Route groups: `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`, `(public)`
- Public event page: `src/app/(public)/e/[slug]/page.tsx`
- Protected dashboard: `src/app/(dashboard)/**` guarded by middleware
- Use `generateMetadata` for SEO on public pages
- Call `revalidatePath` after mutations (in Server Actions, not components)

## UI Standards

- Use design tokens from `docs/10_UI_SYSTEM.md` — no hardcoded hex colors
- Dark mode default; support light via `next-themes`
- Mobile-first: test at 375px width; 44px min touch targets
- Every list view needs: loading (Skeleton), empty (EmptyState), error (ErrorState)
- shadcn/ui for primitives; domain components per `docs/11_COMPONENT_LIBRARY.md`

## Anti-Patterns

- No `useEffect` for initial data fetch — use Server Components
- No inline styles except dynamic values
- No client-side Supabase for reads that can be server-side
